{"id":"word:hebrew:H4264","type":"word","title":"מַחֲנֶה","subtitle":"H4264 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"an encampment (of travellers or troops); hence, an army , whether literal (of soldiers) or figurative (of dancers, angels, cattle, locusts, stars; or even the sacred courts)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מַחֲנֶה (H4264) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 216 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מַחֲנֶה (machăneh) means an encampment (of travellers or troops); hence, an army , whether literal (of soldiers) or figurative (of dancers, angels, cattle, locusts, stars; or even the sacred courts) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 9 18."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מַחֲנֶה","transliteration":"machăneh","pronunciation":"makh-an-eh'","strong":"H4264","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4264","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["מַחֲנֵ֣ה","הַֽ/מַּחֲנֶ֔ה","הַֽ/מַּחֲנֶֽה","הַֽ/מַּחֲנֶ֑ה","הַֽ/מַּחֲנֶ֖ה"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncbsa",69],["HRd/Ncbsa",54],["HNcbsc",34],["HR/Ncbsc",17],["HNcbpc/Sp3mp",7],["HNcbsc/Sp3ms",6],["HTd/Ncbpa",6],["HC/Ncbsc",3],["HNcbsa",3],["HNcbpa",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"an encampment (of travellers or troops); hence, an army , whether literal (of soldiers) or figurative (of dancers, angels, cattle, locusts, stars; or even the sacred courts)","usage":"army, band, battle, camp, company, drove, host, tents.","full":"H4264. machaneh מַחֲנֶה 214 noun masculine Gen 33:8 16t. and feminine Psa 27:3 ; 1Chr 11:15 (on Gen 32:9 a see Di) encampment, camp — absolute ׳מ 32:9 (twice in verse) + 126 t. (including Ezek 1:24 , strike out Co); construct מַחֲנֵה Gen 32:3 56t.; suffix מַחֲנֵהוּ Num 1:52 5 t.; מַחֲנֶיךָ Deut 23:15 ; 29:10 , מַחֲנֶךָ 23:15 , מַחֲנֵיכֶם Amos 4:10 , מַהֲנֵיהֶם Num 5:3 ; Judg 8:10 (compare below, and on form of noun with suffix see Ges § 93 . 3, R 3); plural absolute מִחֲנות Gen 32:8-9 t.; construct 1Chr 9:18 2 t., מַחֲנִים Num 13:19 ; suffix (apparetnly plural noun) מַחֲנֵיהֶם Josh 10:4-5 t.; — on dual see ׳מ proper name below 1 camp, place of encampment: a. of caravan of travelers Gen 32:22 (J), especially of Israel at Exodus and in wilderness Exod 16:13 (twice in verse); 19:16-17 , (all P; distinguished from עַם ); מ ׳שַׁעַר 32:26 (JE); especially המ ׳מִחוּץ in connection with uncleanness, etc., 29:14 ; Lev 4:12 (P) + often, of position of tent of meeting Exod 33:7 (twice in verse) (JE), contr. Num 2:17 (P), where of encampments of several tribes, compare 1:52 ; 2:3 ; 10:2 , 5 , 6 , 25 etc., (all P), already passing over to 3 (compare הַחֹנִים Num 10:5-6 ,); specifically of camp of Levites , surrounding tabernacle, so that P can say הַלְוִיִם מַחֲנֵה אֹהֶלמֿוֺעֵד 2:17 ; and so (late) of temple לֵוִי בְּנֵי לְמַחֲנוֺת הַשֹּׁעֲרִים 1Chr 9:18 , as well as י מַחֲנוֺת ׳שַׁעֲרֵי 2Chr 31:2 ; plural (opposed to מִבְצָרִים = fortresses ) Num 13:19 . 2 camp of armed host Josh 6:11 (twice in verse); 6:14 (JE), 1Sam 4:3 , 5 , 6 (twice in verse); 4:7 ; 17:53 ; 2Kin 7:16 etc. 3. a. those who encamp Num 10:5-6 , 1Chr 11:15 ; Psa 27:3 (all with verb חנה ) compare (probably) Isa 37:36 = 2Kin 19:35 , etc. b. company, body of people ; people and beasts Gen 32:8 ; 32:9 (twice in verse); 32:11 ; 33:8 , funeral company of Jacob 50:9 ; of Israel on march Exod 14:19-20 , compare Num 10:5-6 ,. c. army, host Josh 8:13 ; 10:5 ; 11:4 ; Judg 4:15-16 , (twice in verse); 7:1 , 8 ; 8:10 (twice in verse); 8:11 (twice in verse); 8:12 ; 1Sam 17:1 , 46 ; 2Kin 3:9 even while in the thick of the fight; 1Kin 22:34 2Chr 18:33 etc.","rootNote":"from 2583 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 9 18","keyReferences":["1Chr 9 18","1Chr 9 19","1Chr 11 15","1Chr 11 18","1Chr 12 23","1Chr 12 23","1Chr 14 15","1Chr 14 16"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":216,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Ch